I've begun writing a patch which would introduce plant elementals to 
NetHack.

What's a plant elemental? Think Swamp Thing from comic books.

So far I have the patch working where a plant elemental will be generated 
if a swamp room is generated on a level, in Juiblex's lair and on Medusa. 
Beyond these special rooms, figurines and reverse genocides plant 
elementals are not randomly generated in game.

The patch works except when it comes to a swamp room there will be MANY 
generated instead of just one or two. Having a plant elemental generated on 
Juiblex's Lair and Medusa was much easier to do. Would someone suggest a 
fix for mkroom.c?

There's one thing I want to put in the patch and it appears I'm doing it 
wrong and need some hand holding.

Swamp Thing is a plant who thinks it is a man, formerly Alec Holland (see 
The Anatomy Lesson, Swamp Thing #21). What I had envisioned is that a 
player killed by a plant elemental would rise up as one in a bones file. 
The bit of code that I was going to add to end.c was:

    	else if (mtmp->data == &mons[PM_PLANT_ELEMENTAL])
	u.ugrave.arise = PM_PLANT_ELEMENTAL;

Unfortunately it appears that isn't good enough and the code makes my 
compiler cranky at me for fumbling around blindly with the source.

Anyway here's my preliminary patch to add swamp thi^H^H^H^H^H^H^H^H^H plant 
elementals to the game.

